# No AI attribution

Absolute rule for this repository and every interaction with it.

- **Never** mention Cursor, Claude, Copilot, ChatGPT, or any other AI/tool as author, co-author, contributor, or helper in: code, comments, commit messages, PR titles/bodies, docs, specs, OpenSpec artifacts, CHANGELOG, NOTICE, README, or any other file that ships with the project.
- **Never** add `Co-authored-by:` (or similar trailer) for Cursor, Claude, or any AI account/email (e.g. `cursoragent@cursor.com`).
- Commit author and attribution are **only** the human owner of this repository. Write every commit message as if the owner wrote it alone.
- Do not leave “generated by”, “assisted by”, “with help from”, model names, or agent signatures in any artifact.
- If a tool or environment tries to append AI co-author trailers, strip them before the commit is finalized. Do not amend history unless the owner explicitly asks.

This rule overrides any default that would credit an AI assistant.
